---
// src/pages/medical.astro
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Medical Horizons - Neurobotics">
  <!-- HERO BANNER WITH DNA MORPH VIDEO -->
  <section class="spec-hero-section">
    <video autoplay loop muted playsinline class="spec-hero-video">
      <source src="/assets/videos/finished-neurobotics-medical-horizons-video.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
    </video>

    <div class="spec-hero-overlay"></div>

    <div class="spec-hero-content fade-in">
      <img src="/assets/images/science-neural-owl-logo-steampunk.png" alt="Neural Owl Logo" class="glaux-hero-badge">
      
      <div class="spec-hero-text">
        <span class="spec-id-tag">NEUROBOTICS BIO-CYBERNETICS</span>
        <h1 class="spec-hero-title">Medical Horizons</h1>
        <p class="spec-hero-subtitle">Custom ASIC Miniaturization & Deterministic Neuroprosthetics</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MANIFESTO & ARCHITECTURE BODY -->
  <section class="manifesto-body-section">
    <div class="manifesto-body-container">
      
      <!-- INTRO BLOCK -->
      <div class="spec-intro-block">
        <h2>The Silicon Horizon</h2>
        <hr class="spec-divider">
        <p class="spec-lead-text">
          While the current Neurobotics architecture operates on sub-15W printed circuit boards, the ultimate roadmap compresses the 7-Tier S-M-R Matrix into a custom System-on-Chip (SoC). This transition shrinks the hardware footprint from inches to millimeters and reduces power demands to milliwatt thresholds. This extreme efficiency enables long-term battery operation or passive bio-galvanic energy harvesting for minimally invasive medical implants.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- THREE PILLARS GRID -->
      <div class="pillars-grid">
        
        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">01</div>
          <h3>Neural Bridging</h3>
          <p>
            By utilizing Tier 1 spinal reflex arcs, a millimetric Neurobotics MCU can bridge severed spinal cord regions to read biological nerve impulses and execute real-time motor outputs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">02</div>
          <h3>Neurological Stabilization</h3>
          <p>
            Miniaturized implants utilizing homeostatic state tracking (Tier 2) can detect precursors to tremors or seizures, deploying localized micro-stimulation to stabilize patients.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-icon">03</div>
          <h3>Galvanic Shielding</h3>
          <p>
            Neurobotics' Board Four optoisolated shielding isolates delicate neural interfaces from high-voltage actuator spikes, ensuring flawless signal integrity across the brain-prosthetic barrier.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- TECHNICAL SPECS TABLE -->
      <div class="spec-table-container">
        <h3>System Architecture Parameters</h3>
        <table class="spec-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Parameter</th>
              <th>Specification</th>
              <th>Clinical Impact</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Target Substrate</strong></td>
              <td>Custom System-on-Chip (SoC)</td>
              <td>Compresses the entire 7-Tier cognitive matrix into a millimetric footprint for safe biological embedding.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Power Consumption</strong></td>
              <td>Sub-Milliwatt Thresholds</td>
              <td>Shrinks power needs from watts to milliwatts, facilitating passive bio-galvanic energy harvesting.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Noise Isolation</strong></td>
              <td>Optoisolated Board Four</td>
              <td>Eliminates actuator motor spikes from corrupting neural sensor readings in brain-computer interfaces.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Validation Methodology</strong></td>
              <td>Deterministic Digital Twin</td>
              <td>Allows pharmaceutical labs to test neural stress and BCIs entirely inside silicon without animal testing.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- QUOTE CALLOUT BLOCK -->
      <blockquote class="manifesto-quote">
        "By providing the medical community with an open-source, deterministic hardware baseline, we can accelerate the end of animal testing in neurological science."
      </blockquote>

      <!-- ARCHIVAL PROOF & CORE MANIFESTOS -->
      <section class="proof-section">
        <div class="proof-header">
          <span class="section-tag">STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</span>
          <h2>The "Silicon Twin" & Medical Partnerships</h2>
          <p class="proof-subtitle">Accelerating human clinical deployment through cruelty-free architecture validation and dual-licensed IP integration.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- NEW 3-COLUMN GRID -->
        <div class="proof-grid-3">
          
          <!-- 1. Cruelty-Free Validation -->
          <div class="proof-card">
            <div class="card-meta">
              <span class="log-id">IN SILICO VALIDATION</span>
              <span class="status-badge">ETHICS</span>
            </div>
            <h4>Cruelty-Free "Silicon Twin"</h4>
            <p>Because the SBALF architecture directly mirrors biological nervous systems, it functions as a deterministic digital twin of biological neurology. This guarantees flawless repeatability and allows researchers to test intent-driven decoders without animal testing.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- 2. Dual Licensing -->
          <div class="proof-card">
            <div class="card-meta">
              <span class="log-id">DUAL-LICENSING</span>
              <span class="status-badge">BUSINESS</span>
            </div>
            <h4>Open Science & Commercial Integration</h4>
            <p>We offer open-source access (AGPL-3.0) to lower-nervous-system schematics for university research, alongside Master Commercial Licenses that let medical manufacturers retain sole ownership of their proprietary hardware.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- 3. Briefing PDF -->
          <a href="/assets/docs/neurobotics-medical-horizons-fact-sheet.pdf" class="proof-card" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <div class="card-meta">
              <span class="log-id">NBPR-2026-MEDICAL</span>
              <span class="status-badge">DOWNLOAD</span>
            </div>
            <h4>Medical Potential & Miniaturization</h4>
            <p>Read the official public briefing detailing our roadmap for custom ASIC miniaturization, neuroprosthetics, and the elimination of in vivo testing.</p>
          </a>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- KNOCKOUT VIDEO MASK -->
      <div class="video-text-wrapper">
        <video autoplay loop muted playsinline class="text-video-bg">
          <source src="/assets/videos/deep-space-cosmic-nebula-with-vibrant-purple-and-blue.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
        
        <div class="knockout-overlay">
          <h1 class="video-masked-text">ESSE QUAM VIDERI</h1>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* --- HERO SECTION STYLES --- */
  .spec-hero-section {
    height: 60vh;
    min-height: 450px;
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a3a;
  }

  .spec-hero-video {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0;
    width: 100%; height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    z-index: 0;
  }

  .spec-hero-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(3, 3, 10, 0.4) 0%, rgba(3, 3, 10, 0.9) 100%);
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .spec-hero-content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 40px;
    max-width: 1200px;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0 40px;
  }

  .glaux-hero-badge {
    width: 175px;
    height: auto;
    filter: drop-shadow(0px 0px 20px rgba(153, 103, 151, 0.28));
  }

  .spec-id-tag {
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    color: #00e5ff;
    font-weight: 700;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .spec-hero-title {
    font-size: 4.5rem;
    font-family: 'Aldrich', sans-serif;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .spec-hero-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    color: #d0d8e8;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-weight: 300;
  }

  /* --- MANIFESTO BODY STYLES --- */
  .manifesto-body-section {
    background-color: #03030a;
    padding: 80px 40px;
    color: #e0e0e0;
  }

  .manifesto-body-container {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .spec-intro-block h2 {
    font-size: 2.8rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .spec-divider {
    border-color: #203554;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }

  .spec-lead-text {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #c5d3e8;
  }

  /* --- PILLARS GRID --- */
  .pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 30px;
    margin: 60px 0;
  }

  .pillar-card {
    background: #080d1a;
    border: 1px solid #1a2a40;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, border-color 0.3s ease;
  }

  .pillar-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-5px);
    border-color: #00e5ff;
  }

  .pillar-icon {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: #d4af37;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .pillar-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .pillar-card p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #a8b8d0;
  }

  /* --- SPEC TABLE --- */
  .spec-table-container {
    margin: 80px 0;
  }

  .spec-table-container h3 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-bottom: 25px;
  }

  .spec-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    background: #050914;
    border: 1px solid #1a2a40;
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .spec-table th, .spec-table td {
    padding: 18px 25px;
    text-align: left;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #101c2e;
  }

  .spec-table th {
    background-color: #0b1426;
    color: #00e5ff;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .spec-table td {
    color: #d0d8e8;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  /* --- QUOTE CALLOUT --- */
  .manifesto-quote {
    border-left: 4px solid #d4af37;
    background: #080d1a;
    padding: 30px 40px;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin: 60px 0;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
  }

  /* --- KNOCKOUT VIDEO MASK --- */
  .video-text-wrapper {
    position: relative;
    margin-top: 60px;
    height: 120px;
    overflow: hidden;
    width: 60%;
    margin-left: auto;
    background-color: #000000;
    mix-blend-mode: screen;
  }

  .text-video-bg {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%; left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    min-width: 100%; min-height: 100%;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .knockout-overlay {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;
    background-color: #000000;
    color: #ffffff;
    mix-blend-mode: multiply;
    z-index: 2;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .video-masked-text {
    font-size: 3.5rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    letter-spacing: 5px;
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  /* --- ANIMATIONS --- */
  .fade-in {
    animation: fadeInAnimation 1.5s ease-out forwards;
  }

  @keyframes fadeInAnimation {
    0% { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(30px); }
    100% { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }

  /* --- PROOF SECTION --- */
  .proof-section {
    margin: 4rem 0 2rem 0;
    width: 100%;
    background: rgba(10, 15, 25, 0.4); 
    padding: 2.5rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.1);
  }

  .proof-header {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .section-tag {
    color: #00e5ff;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .proof-header h2 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }

  .proof-subtitle {
    color: #a0aec0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  /* UPDATED: 3-Column Grid Layout */
  .proof-grid-3 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .proof-grid-3 {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .proof-grid-3 {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .proof-card {
    background: #090d16;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.2);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .proof-card:hover {
    background: #0d1424;
    border-color: #00e5ff;
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.15);
  }

  .card-meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .log-id {
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #00e5ff;
  }

  .status-badge {
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    background: rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.05);
    color: #00e5ff;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 229, 255, 0.2);
  }

  .proof-card h4 {
    color: #ffffff;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .proof-card p {
    color: #a0aec0;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>